#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-quota-price — the price list as CODE (USAGE_TELEMETRY_100P §4 M4, §3.1 L3).

WHY THIS EXISTS. The fleet has a good NUMERATOR (what tokens we moved — every transcript records
it) and a good DENOMINATOR (what quota we are allowed — `account-utilization.jsonl` samples
`api/oauth/usage` every ~6 min), and until now it had NOTHING THAT CONVERTS BETWEEN THEM. That
converter is the price list, and USAGE_TELEMETRY_100P §3.1 names it "the actual deliverable":
without it, every cost claim in this repo is unpriced, and a token census can only report the
class that costs nothing. §2.2's governing fact — ~97% of the tokens this fleet moves cost ~0% of
its quota — is *only* visible through this join.

The plan's price list was fitted BY HAND, once, in a research wave, and the hand fit was wrong
until it was corrected twice (§2.1). This file is that arithmetic made re-runnable, with the bug
that corrupted it turned into a tested invariant.

🚨 THE INVARIANT THIS FILE EXISTS TO HOLD — DEDUPE ON `message.id` OR BE WRONG BY 2.4x.
Claude Code writes a streaming assistant message to the transcript ONCE PER CONTENT BLOCK: same
`message.id`, same `requestId`, and the identical COMPLETE `usage` object on every one of them.
A census that sums records therefore counts one billing event 2-3x. Measured in this corpus
(§2.1): 58.7% repeat records, 98.5% byte-identical usage, 0 records spanning files. Three
independent derivations of this wave hit the bug; A1's own falsifier #6 NAMED the hazard and was
not run, and the resulting price list was published 2.1-2.8x too high. `--selftest` case 2
RED-proves the dedup by running the production extractor with the dedup DISABLED (`CC_QP_DEDUP=0`)
and asserting the naive count inflates output >=2x — so if anyone deletes the dedup, case 1 goes
red rather than the number going quietly wrong.

METHOD (and it is the plan's own, so the two agree by construction).
  L1 numerator   walk the transcript roots, dedupe on message.id, sum the four token classes.
  L2 denominator walk account-utilization.jsonl, form (account, bucket) pairs, take
                 Delta weekly_pct across each bucket.
  L3 the join    non-negative least squares through the origin: Delta pp ~ output + cache_creation
                 + input. cache_read is EXCLUDED as a regressor by default and reported as bounded
                 (see below), never as a fitted zero.

WHY BUCKETS AND NOT SAMPLES. `weekly_pct` is an INTEGER percent, so the Delta across one ~6-minute
sample is 0 almost always and the regression would be fitting quantization noise. §2.2's own model
comparison used 67 `(account, 6h)` buckets; this defaults to the same 6h and exposes it as
`--bucket-h`.

WHY cache_read IS NOT A FITTED COEFFICIENT. §2.8 settled the ORDER by experiment (31.7M cache_read
against 208 output moved the weekly meter by 1 point where list pricing demanded 4.62), bounding
cache_read at <=0.018-0.049 pp/Mtok. But `corr(output, cache_read) = +0.909` in observational data
makes the coefficient UNIDENTIFIABLE from a fit, and NNLS is bounded below at zero, so a fitted
0.0000 is a BOUNDARY ARTIFACT and not a measurement — A1's exact zero was exactly that. So this
tool refuses to publish a cache_read coefficient by default: it reports the experimental bound and
the measured collinearity instead. `--with-cache-read` adds the column as a labelled DIAGNOSTIC,
never as the price list.

ABSTAIN, NEVER IMPUTE (design law §3.3.4, carried from CONTEXT_ECONOMY_V2). A missing store, a
window with no movement, too few buckets -> the verdict is ABSTAIN with the reason NAMED, exit 3,
and no numbers. A price list that quietly interpolates over an empty join is the `cc-value` failure
(§2.7) in a new file.

Usage:
  cc-quota-price                    the price list table
  cc-quota-price --json             machine-readable {verdict, price, fit, census, buckets}
  cc-quota-price --census           the deduped token census only (no fit, no denominator needed)
  cc-quota-price --selftest         hermetic RED-provable self-check; exit 1 on any failed case

Options:
  --since <all|Nd|Nh|YYYY-MM-DD>    window (default 7d)
  --bucket-h <N>                    denominator bucket width in hours (default 6)
  --acct <name>                     restrict to one account
  --with-cache-read                 add cache_read as a DIAGNOSTIC column (see above)
  --min-buckets <N>                 abstain below this many moving buckets (default 12)

Config (all env, test-overridable):
  CC_QP_ROOTS        newline/':'-separated transcript roots (default: the 4 real config dirs)
  CC_UTIL_LOG        the utilization series (same override claude-accounts/pool-floor.sh honor)
  CC_QP_MIN_BUCKETS  default for --min-buckets
  CC_QP_MAX_GAP_S    a sample gap wider than this breaks a bucket (default 5400)
  CC_QP_DEDUP        TEST SEAM ONLY. 0 disables the message.id dedup so the selftest can
                     RED-prove it. Prints a loud stderr warning; never set it in production.
  CC_NOW             epoch override for "now" (tests)

Exit: 0 verdict · 1 selftest failure · 2 usage · 3 ABSTAIN (no data / no recoverable denominator).
"""

import glob
import itertools
import json
import os
import sys
import time
from datetime import datetime, timezone

PROG = "cc-quota-price"
HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")

# The four REAL config dirs. ~/.claude-next{,2,3,4}/projects are SYMLINKS into these (§1), so
# naming only the real roots keeps the scan cheap; the walk realpath-dedupes regardless, because a
# double-counted file is the same 2x error the message.id dedup exists to prevent, one level up.
DEFAULT_ROOTS = [
    (os.path.join(HOME, ".claude", "projects"), "next"),
    (os.path.join(HOME, ".claude-secondary", "projects"), "next2"),
    (os.path.join(HOME, ".claude-tertiary", "projects"), "next3"),
    (os.path.join(HOME, ".claude-quaternary", "projects"), "next4"),
]

# config-dir basename -> account. Mirrors lib/account-map.generated.sh
# `cc_acct_name_for_dir_basename`; an unknown basename maps to "" and its tokens are counted in the
# census but can never enter a fit, because no denominator series names that account.
DIR_TO_ACCT = {
    ".claude": "next", "claude": "next", ".claude-next": "next", "claude-next": "next",
    ".claude-secondary": "next2", "claude-secondary": "next2",
    ".claude-tertiary": "next3", "claude-tertiary": "next3",
    ".claude-quaternary": "next4", "claude-quaternary": "next4",
}

CLASSES = ("output", "cache_creation", "input", "cache_read")
# The regressors of the published price list. cache_read is deliberately absent — see the module
# docstring. --with-cache-read appends it as a diagnostic.
FIT_CLASSES = ("output", "cache_creation", "input")


def now_epoch():
    v = os.environ.get("CC_NOW")
    if v:
        try:
            return int(float(v))
        except ValueError:
            pass
    return int(time.time())


def parse_since(spec, now):
    """'all' | '<N>d' | '<N>h' | 'YYYY-MM-DD' -> epoch floor (None for 'all')."""
    if not spec or spec == "all":
        return None
    try:
        if spec.endswith("d"):
            return now - int(float(spec[:-1])) * 86400
        if spec.endswith("h"):
            return now - int(float(spec[:-1])) * 3600
        return int(datetime.strptime(spec, "%Y-%m-%d")
                   .replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc).timestamp())
    except (ValueError, TypeError):
        return None


def iso_to_epoch(s):
    if not isinstance(s, str) or not s:
        return None
    t = s.strip().replace("Z", "+00:00")
    try:
        d = datetime.fromisoformat(t)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if d.tzinfo is None:
        d = d.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)
    return d.timestamp()


# ── L1: the deduped token census ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def transcript_roots():
    """[(dir, acct)] — CC_QP_ROOTS overrides. An override entry is 'path' or 'path=acct'."""
    raw = os.environ.get("CC_QP_ROOTS")
    if not raw:
        return [(d, a) for d, a in DEFAULT_ROOTS if os.path.isdir(d)]
    out = []
    for part in raw.replace(":", "\n").split("\n"):
        part = part.strip()
        if not part:
            continue
        if "=" in part:
            d, acct = part.split("=", 1)
        else:
            d, acct = part, ""
        d = os.path.expanduser(d)
        if not acct:
            # derive from the config-dir basename: <cfg>/projects -> basename(<cfg>)
            acct = DIR_TO_ACCT.get(os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(d))), "")
        if os.path.isdir(d):
            out.append((d, acct))
    return out


def census(since=None, acct_filter=None):
    """Walk the transcript roots and return the DEDUPED per-(acct, epoch) token records.

    Returns (records, meta) where records is a list of
        {"ts": epoch, "acct": str, "model": str, "output":.., "cache_creation":.., ...}
    one per DEDUPED billed response, and meta carries the dedup evidence.

    The dedup key is `message.id`, falling back to `requestId` and then to (file, line) so that a
    record which carries NEITHER is counted once rather than dropped — dropping real billed spend
    would bias the fit low, which is the same fabrication as inventing it, in the other direction.
    """
    dedup = os.environ.get("CC_QP_DEDUP", "1") != "0"
    if not dedup:
        sys.stderr.write(
            f"{PROG}: 🚨 CC_QP_DEDUP=0 — message.id dedup DISABLED. This is a TEST SEAM; the "
            "resulting census over-counts every streamed response 2-3x.\n")

    seen = set()
    recs = []
    meta = {"files": 0, "records": 0, "deduped": 0, "repeats": 0,
            "unkeyed": 0, "models": {}, "roots": []}

    seen_files = set()
    for root, acct in transcript_roots():
        if acct_filter and acct != acct_filter:
            continue
        meta["roots"].append({"dir": root, "acct": acct})
        for f in glob.iglob(os.path.join(root, "**", "*.jsonl"), recursive=True):
            rp = os.path.realpath(f)
            if rp in seen_files:
                continue          # a symlinked root would otherwise contribute every file twice
            seen_files.add(rp)
            # A file last written before the window opened cannot hold an in-window record.
            if since is not None:
                try:
                    if os.stat(rp).st_mtime < since:
                        continue
                except OSError:
                    continue
            meta["files"] += 1
            try:
                fh = open(rp, "rb")
            except OSError:
                continue
            with fh:
                for lineno, line in enumerate(fh):
                    if b'"usage"' not in line:
                        continue
                    try:
                        d = json.loads(line)
                    except (ValueError, UnicodeDecodeError):
                        continue
                    m = d.get("message")
                    if not isinstance(m, dict):
                        continue
                    u = m.get("usage")
                    if not isinstance(u, dict):
                        continue
                    meta["records"] += 1
                    key = m.get("id") or d.get("requestId")
                    if not key:
                        meta["unkeyed"] += 1
                        key = f"{rp}#{lineno}"
                    if dedup:
                        if key in seen:
                            meta["repeats"] += 1
                            continue
                        seen.add(key)
                    ts = iso_to_epoch(d.get("timestamp"))
                    if ts is None:
                        continue
                    if since is not None and ts < since:
                        continue
                    model = m.get("model") or "unknown"
                    meta["models"][model] = meta["models"].get(model, 0) + 1
                    meta["deduped"] += 1
                    recs.append({
                        "ts": ts, "acct": acct, "model": model,
                        "input": int(u.get("input_tokens") or 0),
                        "output": int(u.get("output_tokens") or 0),
                        "cache_creation": int(u.get("cache_creation_input_tokens") or 0),
                        "cache_read": int(u.get("cache_read_input_tokens") or 0),
                    })
    return recs, meta


# ── L2: the denominator — (account, bucket) -> Delta weekly_pct ────────────────────────────────
def util_path():
    return os.environ.get("CC_UTIL_LOG") or os.path.join(
        HOME, ".claude", "logs", "account-utilization.jsonl")


def util_rows(path, since=None, acct_filter=None):
    rows = []
    try:
        fh = open(path, "rb")
    except OSError:
        return rows
    with fh:
        for line in fh:
            try:
                d = json.loads(line)
            except (ValueError, UnicodeDecodeError):
                continue
            acct = d.get("acct")
            if not acct or (acct_filter and acct != acct_filter):
                continue
            if d.get("stale"):
                continue            # "we could not measure" is not "nothing was happening"
            wp = d.get("weekly_pct")
            ts = iso_to_epoch(d.get("ts"))
            if wp is None or ts is None:
                continue
            if since is not None and ts < since:
                continue
            rows.append({"ts": ts, "acct": acct, "weekly_pct": float(wp),
                         "reset": d.get("weekly_reset_at") or ""})
    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r["acct"], r["ts"]))
    return rows


def buckets(urows, bucket_h, max_gap_s):
    """[(acct, t0, t1, delta_pp)] — one per usable bucket.

    A bucket is DROPPED, never repaired, when:
      · it spans a weekly reset (weekly_pct falls, or weekly_reset_at changes) — the counter went
        backwards, so its Delta is not spend. This is the same error class that inverted this
        plan's own premise (§1): a resetting counter read as if it were cumulative.
      · its samples are further apart than max_gap_s — the tokens spent in the gap are unmeasured,
        so the pair prices spend it cannot see.
    """
    width = int(bucket_h * 3600)
    out = []
    by_acct = {}
    for r in urows:
        by_acct.setdefault(r["acct"], []).append(r)
    for acct, rs in sorted(by_acct.items()):
        # group into fixed-width blocks aligned to the epoch so buckets are reproducible
        blocks = {}
        for r in rs:
            blocks.setdefault(int(r["ts"]) // width, []).append(r)
        for _, members in sorted(blocks.items()):
            if len(members) < 2:
                continue
            a, b = members[0], members[-1]
            if b["ts"] - a["ts"] > max_gap_s * len(members):
                continue
            if a["reset"] != b["reset"]:
                continue                      # a reset boundary fell inside this bucket
            gapped = any(members[i + 1]["ts"] - members[i]["ts"] > max_gap_s
                         for i in range(len(members) - 1))
            if gapped:
                continue
            if any(members[i + 1]["weekly_pct"] < members[i]["weekly_pct"]
                   for i in range(len(members) - 1)):
                continue                      # the counter went backwards: a reset, not spend
            out.append((acct, a["ts"], b["ts"], b["weekly_pct"] - a["weekly_pct"]))
    return out


def join(recs, bkts):
    """Sum each bucket's deduped tokens. Returns rows [{acct,t0,t1,dpp,<class>:..,models:{}}]."""
    by_acct = {}
    for r in recs:
        by_acct.setdefault(r["acct"], []).append(r)
    for v in by_acct.values():
        v.sort(key=lambda r: r["ts"])
    rows = []
    for acct, t0, t1, dpp in bkts:
        row = {"acct": acct, "t0": t0, "t1": t1, "dpp": dpp, "n_resp": 0, "models": {}}
        for c in CLASSES:
            row[c] = 0
        for r in by_acct.get(acct, ()):
            if t0 <= r["ts"] <= t1:
                row["n_resp"] += 1
                row["models"][r["model"]] = row["models"].get(r["model"], 0) + r["output"]
                for c in CLASSES:
                    row[c] += r[c]
        rows.append(row)
    return rows


# ── L3: the fit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def _solve(ata, atb):
    """Gaussian elimination with partial pivoting. Returns None on a singular system."""
    n = len(atb)
    m = [list(ata[i]) + [atb[i]] for i in range(n)]
    for col in range(n):
        piv = max(range(col, n), key=lambda r: abs(m[r][col]))
        if abs(m[piv][col]) < 1e-12:
            return None
        m[col], m[piv] = m[piv], m[col]
        pv = m[col][col]
        for r in range(n):
            if r == col:
                continue
            f = m[r][col] / pv
            if f:
                for c in range(col, n + 1):
                    m[r][c] -= f * m[col][c]
    return [m[i][n] / m[i][i] for i in range(n)]


def nnls(A, b):
    """Exact NNLS for a small number of columns, by exhaustive support search.

    The NNLS optimum is the unconstrained least-squares solution on its own support, and that
    solution is nonnegative. So enumerating every subset of columns, keeping the subsets whose
    unconstrained solution is feasible (all coefficients >= 0), and taking the minimum residual
    among them yields the exact optimum. With <= 4 columns that is <= 16 solves — no iteration, so
    no convergence bug to hide a wrong price behind.
    """
    n = len(A[0]) if A else 0
    best, best_rss = [0.0] * n, sum(v * v for v in b)
    for k in range(1, n + 1):
        for S in itertools.combinations(range(n), k):
            ata = [[sum(row[i] * row[j] for row in A) for j in S] for i in S]
            atb = [sum(row[i] * y for row, y in zip(A, b)) for i in S]
            sol = _solve(ata, atb)
            if sol is None or any(v < 0 for v in sol):
                continue
            x = [0.0] * n
            for idx, i in enumerate(S):
                x[i] = sol[idx]
            rss = sum((y - sum(row[i] * x[i] for i in range(n))) ** 2 for row, y in zip(A, b))
            if rss < best_rss - 1e-15:
                best, best_rss = x, rss
    return best, best_rss


def corr(xs, ys):
    n = len(xs)
    if n < 2:
        return None
    mx, my = sum(xs) / n, sum(ys) / n
    sxy = sum((a - mx) * (b - my) for a, b in zip(xs, ys))
    sxx = sum((a - mx) ** 2 for a in xs)
    syy = sum((b - my) ** 2 for b in ys)
    if sxx <= 0 or syy <= 0:
        return None
    return sxy / (sxx * syy) ** 0.5


def fit(rows, cols):
    A = [[float(r[c]) for c in cols] for r in rows]
    b = [float(r["dpp"]) for r in rows]
    x, rss = nnls(A, b)
    tss = sum(v * v for v in b)                       # through the origin: TSS about 0
    r2 = 1.0 - rss / tss if tss > 0 else None
    rel_rmse = ((rss / len(b)) ** 0.5) / (sum(b) / len(b)) if b and sum(b) > 0 else None
    return {
        "coef_pp_per_token": dict(zip(cols, x)),
        "r2": r2, "rel_rmse": rel_rmse, "n": len(b),
        "collinearity": {
            f"{a}~{c}": corr([r[a] for r in rows], [r[c] for r in rows])
            for a, c in itertools.combinations(CLASSES, 2)
        },
    }


# ── verdict assembly ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §2.8's experimental bound on cache_read, quoted rather than fitted. Units: pp per 1M tokens.
CACHE_READ_BOUND_PP_PER_MTOK = 0.049


def build(args):
    now = now_epoch()
    since = parse_since(args["since"], now)
    recs, meta = census(since, args["acct"])
    if args["census_only"]:
        tot = {c: sum(r[c] for r in recs) for c in CLASSES}
        return {"verdict": "CENSUS", "window": args["since"], "census": meta, "tokens": tot}, 0

    up = util_path()
    if not os.path.exists(up):
        return _abstain(f"no denominator: the utilization series {up} does not exist. "
                        "Nothing on this box can convert tokens to weekly points without it.",
                        meta, args), 3
    urows = util_rows(up, since, args["acct"])
    if len(urows) < 2:
        return _abstain(f"no denominator: {len(urows)} usable sample(s) in {up} for window "
                        f"'{args['since']}' (stale rows are excluded by design).", meta, args), 3
    if not recs:
        return _abstain(f"no numerator: 0 billed responses found in {meta['files']} transcript "
                        f"file(s) across {len(meta['roots'])} root(s) for window "
                        f"'{args['since']}'.", meta, args), 3

    bkts = buckets(urows, args["bucket_h"], args["max_gap_s"])
    rows = join(recs, bkts)
    moving = [r for r in rows if r["dpp"] > 0]
    if len(moving) < args["min_buckets"]:
        return _abstain(
            f"insufficient movement: {len(moving)} bucket(s) with a positive "
            f"Delta weekly_pct, below the floor of {args['min_buckets']} "
            f"({len(rows)} bucket(s) formed from {len(urows)} sample(s) at "
            f"{args['bucket_h']}h). weekly_pct is an INTEGER percent, so a short or quiet "
            "window genuinely cannot price anything — widen --since or --bucket-h.",
            meta, args, extra={"buckets_formed": len(rows), "buckets_moving": len(moving)}), 3

    cols = list(FIT_CLASSES) + (["cache_read"] if args["with_cache_read"] else [])
    f = fit(moving, cols)

    price = {}
    for c in cols:
        pp_per_tok = f["coef_pp_per_token"][c]
        price[c] = {
            "pp_per_mtok": pp_per_tok * 1e6,
            "tokens_per_pp": (1.0 / pp_per_tok) if pp_per_tok > 0 else None,
            "kind": "fitted" if c in FIT_CLASSES else "diagnostic",
        }
    if not args["with_cache_read"]:
        price["cache_read"] = {
            "pp_per_mtok": None,
            "tokens_per_pp": None,
            "kind": "bounded",
            "bound_pp_per_mtok": CACHE_READ_BOUND_PP_PER_MTOK,
            "why": "NOT FITTED. §2.8 bounded it by experiment at <=0.018-0.049 pp/Mtok; "
                   "observationally it is collinear with output (r~+0.91), so a fitted value "
                   "would be a boundary artifact, not a measurement.",
        }

    mix = {}
    for r in moving:
        for m, v in r["models"].items():
            mix[m] = mix.get(m, 0) + v
    tot_out = sum(mix.values()) or 1
    dominant = max(mix.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]) if mix else ("unknown", 0)
    blended = dominant[1] / tot_out < 0.90

    return {
        "verdict": "OK",
        "window": args["since"], "bucket_h": args["bucket_h"],
        "price": price,
        "fit": f,
        "census": meta,
        "buckets": {"formed": len(rows), "moving": len(moving),
                    "samples": len(urows), "min_required": args["min_buckets"]},
        "model_mix": {m: v / tot_out for m, v in sorted(mix.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1])},
        "blended": blended,
        "caveats": ([
            f"BLENDED PRICE — the dominant model is only {dominant[1] / tot_out:.0%} of fitted "
            "output tokens, so these coefficients describe a mix, not one model."
        ] if blended else []) + ([
            "cache_read is included as a DIAGNOSTIC only — it is collinear with output and NNLS "
            "is bounded below at zero, so neither a positive value nor a 0.0000 here is evidence."
        ] if args["with_cache_read"] else []),
    }, 0


def _abstain(reason, meta, args, extra=None):
    d = {"verdict": "ABSTAIN", "reason": reason, "window": args["since"], "census": meta}
    if extra:
        d.update(extra)
    return d


# ── renderer ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def render(d):
    v = d["verdict"]
    if v == "ABSTAIN":
        print(f"{PROG}: ABSTAIN — {d['reason']}")
        print("  (abstain, never impute — design law §3.3.4. No price is reported.)")
        return
    if v == "CENSUS":
        t = d["tokens"]
        m = d["census"]
        print(f"deduped token census — window {d['window']} · {m['files']} file(s) · "
              f"{m['deduped']} billed response(s)")
        for c in CLASSES:
            print(f"  {c:<15s} {t[c]:>18,}")
        if m["records"]:
            print(f"  dedup: {m['repeats']:,} of {m['records']:,} record(s) were repeats "
                  f"({m['repeats'] / m['records']:.1%}) — summing lines would have "
                  f"over-counted by {m['records'] / max(m['deduped'], 1):.2f}x")
        return

    b, f = d["buckets"], d["fit"]
    print(f"quota price list — window {d['window']} · {b['moving']} moving bucket(s) of "
          f"{b['formed']} at {d['bucket_h']}h · R² {f['r2']:.3f}"
          + (f" · rel-RMSE {f['rel_rmse']:.3f}" if f["rel_rmse"] is not None else ""))
    print()
    print(f"  {'class':<15s} {'pp / Mtok':>12s} {'tokens / 1 pp':>16s}   basis")
    for c in CLASSES:
        p = d["price"].get(c)
        if not p:
            continue
        if p["pp_per_mtok"] is None:
            print(f"  {c:<15s} {'—':>12s} {'—':>16s}   bounded <= "
                  f"{p['bound_pp_per_mtok']} pp/Mtok (§2.8, by experiment)")
        else:
            tpp = f"{p['tokens_per_pp']:,.0f}" if p["tokens_per_pp"] else "—"
            print(f"  {c:<15s} {p['pp_per_mtok']:>12.3f} {tpp:>16s}   {p['kind']}")
    print()
    print("  model mix: " + ", ".join(f"{m} {s:.0%}" for m, s in
                                      list(d["model_mix"].items())[:4]))
    cr = f["collinearity"].get("output~cache_read")
    if cr is not None:
        print(f"  corr(output, cache_read) = {cr:+.3f}"
              + ("   ⚠ collinear — cache_read is unidentifiable from this data"
                 if abs(cr) > 0.7 else ""))
    for c in d["caveats"]:
        print(f"  ⚠ {c}")


# ── selftest ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def _tx_line(ts, mid, model, out, cc, cr, inp):
    return json.dumps({
        "type": "assistant", "timestamp": ts, "requestId": "req_" + mid,
        "message": {"id": mid, "model": model, "usage": {
            "input_tokens": inp, "output_tokens": out,
            "cache_creation_input_tokens": cc, "cache_read_input_tokens": cr}},
    }) + "\n"


def _util_line(ts, acct, wp, reset="2026-08-23T00:00:00Z", stale=False):
    return json.dumps({"ts": ts, "acct": acct, "weekly_pct": wp,
                       "weekly_reset_at": reset, "stale": stale}) + "\n"


def _iso(e):
    return datetime.fromtimestamp(e, timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def _run(argv, env):
    """Run this very file in a child with a fixtured environment; return (rc, parsed-json)."""
    import subprocess
    e = dict(os.environ)
    e.update({k: str(v) for k, v in env.items()})
    p = subprocess.run([sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__)] + argv,
                       capture_output=True, text=True, env=e)
    try:
        return p.returncode, json.loads(p.stdout), p.stderr
    except ValueError:
        return p.returncode, None, p.stdout + p.stderr


def selftest():
    import shutil
    import tempfile
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-quota-price-selftest.")
    npass = nfail = 0

    def check(name, ok, detail=""):
        nonlocal npass, nfail
        if ok:
            npass += 1
            print(f"  ok   {name}")
        else:
            nfail += 1
            print(f"  FAIL {name}" + (f"   [{detail}]" if detail else ""))

    try:
        T = 1787000000                        # frozen "now"; every fixture stamp is relative
        root = os.path.join(tmp, ".claude-secondary", "projects", "proj")
        os.makedirs(root)
        util = os.path.join(tmp, "util.jsonl")
        base_env = {"CC_NOW": T, "CC_UTIL_LOG": util,
                    "CC_QP_ROOTS": os.path.join(tmp, ".claude-secondary", "projects") + "=next2"}

        # ── fixture A: ONE billed response, written as THREE streamed lines (the real shape) ──
        # Same message.id, same requestId, identical complete usage on every line — exactly what
        # Claude Code writes per content block. True output for the session is 1000, not 3000.
        with open(os.path.join(root, "a.jsonl"), "w") as fh:
            for _ in range(3):
                fh.write(_tx_line(_iso(T - 3600), "msg_AAA", "claude-opus-5",
                                  out=1000, cc=5000, cr=900000, inp=10))
            fh.write(_tx_line(_iso(T - 3500), "msg_BBB", "claude-opus-5",
                              out=500, cc=2000, cr=800000, inp=10))

        rc, d, err = _run(["--census", "--json", "--since", "1d"], base_env)
        check("1  census dedupes on message.id (3 streamed lines = 1 billed response)",
              rc == 0 and d and d["tokens"]["output"] == 1500 and d["census"]["deduped"] == 2,
              f"rc={rc} got={d and d['tokens']['output']}")

        # ── case 2: the RED-PROOF for case 1. Flip the production dedup off via its test seam
        # and assert the naive census inflates output >=2x. If anyone deletes the dedup, case 1
        # goes red; if anyone weakens this assertion, case 2 goes red. The invariant is live.
        env2 = dict(base_env, CC_QP_DEDUP=0)
        rc2, d2, err2 = _run(["--census", "--json", "--since", "1d"], env2)
        naive = d2["tokens"]["output"] if d2 else 0
        check("2  RED-PROOF: a NON-deduping extractor inflates output >=2x",
              rc2 == 0 and naive >= 2 * 1500,
              f"naive={naive} deduped=1500 ratio={naive / 1500 if naive else 0:.2f}x")
        check("2b RED-PROOF names its own seam loudly on stderr",
              "CC_QP_DEDUP=0" in (err2 or ""), (err2 or "")[:80])

        # ── case 3: absent denominator ⇒ ABSTAIN with the path named, exit 3, valid json ──
        # The reason must name WHICH rung fired ("does not exist"), not merely the path: an
        # empty store and an absent one are different facts, and a reason that cannot tell them
        # apart lets the absent-store guard be deleted without any case going red (found by
        # mutation — the first version of this assertion survived exactly that deletion).
        rc3, d3, _ = _run(["--json", "--since", "1d"],
                          dict(base_env, CC_UTIL_LOG=os.path.join(tmp, "nope.jsonl")))
        check("3  absent utilization store ⇒ ABSTAIN(exit 3), reason names the path AND the rung",
              rc3 == 3 and d3 and d3["verdict"] == "ABSTAIN" and "nope.jsonl" in d3["reason"]
              and "does not exist" in d3["reason"],
              f"rc={rc3} v={d3 and d3['verdict']} r={(d3 or {}).get('reason', '')[:90]}")
        # 3b the OTHER denominator rung: the store exists but carries too few usable samples
        empty = os.path.join(tmp, "empty.jsonl")
        open(empty, "w").close()
        rc3b, d3b, _ = _run(["--json", "--since", "1d"], dict(base_env, CC_UTIL_LOG=empty))
        check("3b present-but-empty store ⇒ a DIFFERENT abstain reason, not the absent-store one",
              rc3b == 3 and d3b["verdict"] == "ABSTAIN"
              and "usable sample" in d3b["reason"] and "does not exist" not in d3b["reason"],
              (d3b or {}).get("reason", "")[:90])

        # ── fixture B: a priceable corpus. 24 buckets, each with a KNOWN token vector, and a
        # Delta weekly_pct synthesized from a KNOWN coefficient vector so the fit has a truth to
        # be checked against. out=4 pp/Mtok, cc=0.3 pp/Mtok, in=0 — and cache_read moves with
        # output (the real corpus's +0.91 collinearity) while contributing nothing.
        C_OUT, C_CC = 4.0e-6, 0.3e-6
        # Bucket starts are ALIGNED to the 6h epoch blocks the producer itself uses. An unaligned
        # fixture straddles two blocks, splitting every bucket's samples from its tokens — which is
        # how this case first went red, and is worth keeping as a note: the alignment is part of
        # the contract, not an artifact of the test.
        BW = 6 * 3600
        with open(util, "w") as uh, open(os.path.join(root, "b.jsonl"), "w") as th:
            wp = 0.0
            for i in range(24):
                t0 = (T // BW - (30 - i)) * BW
                out = 40000 + 7000 * (i % 5)
                cc = 900000 + 130000 * (i % 3)
                dpp = out * C_OUT + cc * C_CC
                # samples every 30 min across the 6h bucket; the pct rises only at the close, as
                # an integer-percent meter really does
                for s in range(12):
                    uh.write(_util_line(_iso(t0 + s * 1800), "next2", wp))
                uh.write(_util_line(_iso(t0 + 5 * 3600 + 3000), "next2", wp + dpp))
                wp += dpp
                th.write(_tx_line(_iso(t0 + 600), f"msg_B{i}", "claude-opus-5",
                                  out=out, cc=cc, cr=out * 300, inp=100))

        rc4, d4, err4 = _run(["--json", "--since", "10d", "--bucket-h", "6"], base_env)
        ok4 = rc4 == 0 and d4 and d4["verdict"] == "OK"
        got_out = d4["price"]["output"]["pp_per_mtok"] if ok4 else None
        got_cc = d4["price"]["cache_creation"]["pp_per_mtok"] if ok4 else None
        check("4  fit recovers a KNOWN price list within 5%",
              ok4 and abs(got_out - 4.0) / 4.0 < 0.05 and abs(got_cc - 0.3) / 0.3 < 0.05,
              f"rc={rc4} out={got_out} cc={got_cc} err={(err4 or '')[:120]}")

        # ── case 5: NON-DEGENERACY. Case 4 must be capable of failing — a tolerance that accepts
        # anything proves nothing. Assert the SAME check rejects a price it was not fitted to.
        check("5  NON-DEGENERACY: case 4's tolerance rejects a wrong price (mutant)",
              ok4 and not (abs(got_out - 8.0) / 8.0 < 0.05),
              f"out={got_out}")

        # ── case 6: cache_read is reported as BOUNDED, never as a fitted coefficient ──
        # It must not merely be LABELLED bounded — it must never have been a REGRESSOR, or a
        # boundary-artifact zero is still being computed and one line from being published.
        cr6 = d4["price"]["cache_read"] if ok4 else {}
        check("6  cache_read is 'bounded', not fitted, and never entered the design matrix",
              cr6.get("kind") == "bounded" and cr6.get("pp_per_mtok") is None
              and cr6.get("bound_pp_per_mtok") == CACHE_READ_BOUND_PP_PER_MTOK
              and ok4 and "cache_read" not in d4["fit"]["coef_pp_per_token"],
              str(cr6)[:120])
        # ...and the diagnostic flag labels it as such rather than promoting it to the price list
        rc6b, d6b, _ = _run(["--json", "--since", "10d", "--with-cache-read"], base_env)
        check("6b --with-cache-read labels the column DIAGNOSTIC and says why",
              rc6b == 0 and d6b["price"]["cache_read"]["kind"] == "diagnostic"
              and any("DIAGNOSTIC" in c for c in d6b["caveats"]),
              str(d6b and d6b["price"]["cache_read"])[:120])

        # ── case 7: a bucket spanning a weekly RESET is DROPPED, not read as negative spend.
        # This is the §1 error class — a resetting counter read as if it were cumulative.
        with open(util, "a") as uh:
            t0 = (T // BW - 3) * BW
            for s in range(12):
                uh.write(_util_line(_iso(t0 + s * 1800), "next2", 90.0 - s))   # falls: a reset
            uh.write(_util_line(_iso(t0 + 5 * 3600 + 3000), "next2", 95.0))
        rc7, d7, _ = _run(["--json", "--since", "10d"], base_env)
        check("7  a bucket whose weekly_pct FALLS (a reset) is dropped, not priced",
              rc7 == 0 and d7["buckets"]["moving"] == d4["buckets"]["moving"],
              f"before={d4 and d4['buckets']['moving']} after={d7 and d7['buckets']['moving']}")

        # ── case 8: stale rows are excluded — "could not measure" != "nothing happened" ──
        with open(util, "a") as uh:
            t0 = (T // BW - 2) * BW
            for s in range(12):
                uh.write(_util_line(_iso(t0 + s * 1800), "next2", 95.0, stale=True))
            uh.write(_util_line(_iso(t0 + 5 * 3600 + 3000), "next2", 99.0, stale=True))
        rc8, d8, _ = _run(["--json", "--since", "10d"], base_env)
        check("8  stale utilization rows never enter a bucket",
              rc8 == 0 and d8["buckets"]["moving"] == d4["buckets"]["moving"],
              f"{d8 and d8['buckets']}")

        # ── case 9: too few moving buckets ⇒ ABSTAIN naming the count and the floor ──
        rc9, d9, _ = _run(["--json", "--since", "10d", "--min-buckets", "500"], base_env)
        check("9  below the bucket floor ⇒ ABSTAIN(exit 3) naming the count AND the floor",
              rc9 == 3 and d9["verdict"] == "ABSTAIN" and "500" in d9["reason"]
              and str(d9["buckets_moving"]) in d9["reason"],
              f"rc={rc9} {(d9 or {}).get('reason', '')[:100]}")

        # ── case 10: the table renderer never crashes and never invents a number on ABSTAIN ──
        import subprocess
        e = dict(os.environ)
        e.update({k: str(v) for k, v in base_env.items()})
        e["CC_UTIL_LOG"] = os.path.join(tmp, "nope.jsonl")
        p = subprocess.run([sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), "--since", "1d"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, env=e)
        check("10 ABSTAIN renders a reason and no price table",
              p.returncode == 3 and "ABSTAIN" in p.stdout and "pp / Mtok" not in p.stdout,
              p.stdout[:120])

    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)

    print(f"\n{PROG} --selftest: {npass} passed, {nfail} failed")
    return 1 if nfail else 0


# ── main ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def main(argv):
    args = {
        "json": False, "census_only": False, "since": "7d", "bucket_h": 6.0,
        "acct": None, "with_cache_read": False,
        "min_buckets": int(os.environ.get("CC_QP_MIN_BUCKETS", "12")),
        "max_gap_s": int(os.environ.get("CC_QP_MAX_GAP_S", "5400")),
    }
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a == "--json":
            args["json"] = True
        elif a == "--census":
            args["census_only"] = True
        elif a == "--with-cache-read":
            args["with_cache_read"] = True
        elif a == "--selftest":
            return selftest()
        elif a in ("-h", "--help"):
            sys.stderr.write(__doc__)
            return 2
        elif a in ("--since", "--bucket-h", "--acct", "--min-buckets") and i + 1 < len(argv):
            i += 1
            key = a[2:].replace("-", "_")
            if key == "bucket_h":
                args[key] = float(argv[i])
            elif key == "min_buckets":
                args[key] = int(argv[i])
            else:
                args[key] = argv[i]
        else:
            sys.stderr.write(f"{PROG}: unknown argument {a!r}\n")
            return 2
        i += 1

    d, rc = build(args)
    if args["json"]:
        print(json.dumps(d, separators=(",", ":"), sort_keys=True, default=str))
    else:
        render(d)
    return rc


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
    except BrokenPipeError:
        sys.exit(0)
